# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# research_dataset/.gitignore
#
# The image payloads below are BULK, DERIVED and fully REGENERABLE by the
# collection pipeline from rights-approved sources. They are kept out of Git so
# the repository stays reviewable; the artefacts that record provenance, rights
# determinations and measurements are kept IN Git because those cannot be
# regenerated once the upstream sources change.
#
# To rebuild everything ignored here, from research_dataset/scripts/:
#     ./run_pipeline.sh
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Byte-exact originals (regenerate: python3 collect.py)
raw_images/

# Normalised working copies (regenerate: python3 qc.py)
processed_images/

# Copies routed out by QC, with reasons (regenerate: python3 qc.py)
rejected_images/

# Copies of exact duplicates (regenerate: python3 qc.py)
duplicate_images/

# Generated test fixtures - synthetic, must never enter the corpus
scripts/tests/fixtures/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local caches / partial runs
*.tmp
.cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately TRACKED (do not add these to the ignore list):
#   metadata/            images.csv, sources_registry.*, download_log.jsonl,
#                        qc_records.jsonl, rejected_manifest.csv, sha256_index.json
#   reports/             every generated report
#   annotations/         preserved original annotation files + derived review queue
#   scripts/             the reproducible pipeline itself
#   README.md
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
